  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many pies Smith’s Bakery sold, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the number of pies Mcgee’s Bakery sold.\n2. Use the information given to find out how many pies Smith’s Bakery sold.\n\nStep 1: Identify the number of pies Mcgee’s Bakery sold.\nMcgee’s Bakery sold 16 pies.\n\nStep 2: Use the information given to find out how many pies Smith’s Bakery sold.\nThe problem states that Smith’s Bakery sold 6 more than four times the number of pies that Mcgee’s Bakery sold. We can express this relationship with the following equation:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pies Smith’s Bakery sold} = 4 \\times \\text{Number of pies Mcgee’s Bakery sold} + 6 \\]\n\nSubstitute the number of pies Mcgee’s Bakery sold into the equation:\n\\[ \\text{Number of pies Smith’s Bakery sold} = 4 \\times 16 + 6 \\]\n\nNow, perform the multiplication and addition:\n\\[ 4 \\times 16 = 64 \\]\n\\[ 64 + 6 = 70 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of pies Smith’s Bakery sold is \\(\\boxed{70}\\).",
